      "version": "06/2025",
      "date": "2025-06",
      "url": "https://www.se.com/us/en/download/document/SEPED303002EN/",
      "note": "Addresses in direct-access mode: application, identification, 32-bit and 16-bit metering and diagnosis, status and control zones"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are the word addresses of the manual (hexadecimal), as sent on the wire. Values are read with FC03 or FC04.",
    "32-bit values have the most significant word first. 16-bit signed values are two's complement.",
    "Text values (ASCII) have character n in the low byte and character n+1 in the high byte of each word.",
    "Not in this map: the event tables, the settings and disturbance recording zones (indirect access), the bit-by-bit definitions of the status words, the remote control orders and the 16-bit compatibility zones kept for Sepam 2000."
  ],
